▪ Howto-Enable-Root-Login-on-AWS

This Howto preserves a historical AWS Experiment. It is not a current
All-Dings Deployment Requirement and must not be used as the default
Public-Dings-Server Host setup.

❲Establish-Three-Stage-Dings-Deployment❳❪300101042.md❫ replaces this Ambient
Root-Login Assumption with explicit least-privilege Service ownership,
observable Deployment Planning and recoverable restart behavior. The Commands
below are retained as provenance only.

▪▪ Steps

⌜⌜⌜bash
$ ssh -i /path/my-key-pair.pem ubuntu@ec2-remote-server.amazonaws.com
$ sudo -i bash
$ cp /etc/ssh/sshd_config /etc/ssh/sshd_config.bak
$ vi /etc/ssh/sshd_config
-> PermitRootLogin yes
$ vi ~/.ssh/authorized_keys
-> Remove Line: no-port-forwarding ...
$ passwd root
$ systemctl restart ssh
⌟⌟⌟

